1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,494
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,544 --> 00:00:18,066
The Princess and the Magic Pea!

7
00:00:22,661 --> 00:00:27,903
Once upon a time, in a kingdom of
green hills and sparkling rivers,

8
00:00:27,953 --> 00:00:33,111
there stood a castle made of pale stone,
with yellow windows that glowed like

9
00:00:33,161 --> 00:00:34,547
little suns.

10
00:00:35,173 --> 00:00:37,767
One night, it began to rain.

11
00:00:37,981 --> 00:00:43,208
It rained so much, so very much, that
the raindrops played a little song on

12
00:00:43,258 --> 00:00:44,358
the roof:

13
00:00:44,408 --> 00:00:47,642
pitter, patter, pitter, patter.

14
00:00:48,247 --> 00:00:53,258
Down on the road below, a girl in
a blue cloak was walking along.

15
00:00:53,618 --> 00:00:55,212
Her name was Nina.

16
00:00:55,388 --> 00:01:01,255
And on her shoulder, all huddled up, sat
a teeny-tiny owl with caramel-colored

17
00:01:01,305 --> 00:01:02,505
feathers.

18
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:04,404
Her name was Popcorn.

19
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,211
Hoo, hoo,

20
00:01:06,261 --> 00:01:08,544
said Popcorn, shivering.

21
00:01:08,594 --> 00:01:12,574
Nina, I'm wet all the way
to the tips of my feathers!

22
00:01:13,247 --> 00:01:15,283
Me too, Popcorn,

23
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:16,599
said Nina.

24
00:01:16,649 --> 00:01:17,642
Look!

25
00:01:17,692 --> 00:01:19,381
There's a castle up there.

26
00:01:19,551 --> 00:01:21,372
Let's ask if we can stay.

27
00:01:22,486 --> 00:01:24,400
Knock, knock, knock.

28
00:01:25,065 --> 00:01:27,701
The door was opened by Queen Dorothy.

29
00:01:27,911 --> 00:01:33,111
She was short and round, wore a
nightcap covered in little stars,

30
00:01:33,161 --> 00:01:35,339
and held a candle in her hand.

31
00:01:35,681 --> 00:01:39,094
Peeking out from behind her
was her son, Prince Theo.

32
00:01:39,648 --> 00:01:40,848
Goodness me!

33
00:01:40,898 --> 00:01:42,114
said the queen.

34
00:01:42,164 --> 00:01:43,786
You're soaking wet!

35
00:01:43,974 --> 00:01:45,174
Who are you?

36
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:51,315
I'm Nina, princess of the Kingdom by
the Sea, far away beyond the mountains,

37
00:01:51,365 --> 00:01:52,513
said the girl.

38
00:01:52,563 --> 00:01:54,568
And this is Popcorn.

39
00:01:54,816 --> 00:01:57,019
The storm made us lose our way.

40
00:01:57,676 --> 00:02:00,326
Prince Theo's eyes went wide.

41
00:02:00,742 --> 00:02:01,942
A princess?

42
00:02:02,011 --> 00:02:05,823
But she's dripping wet, and
there's mud all over her shoes!

43
00:02:06,462 --> 00:02:09,070
The queen smiled and gave a wink.

44
00:02:09,373 --> 00:02:14,018
Princess or not, anyone who knocks on
our door on a rainy night deserves a

45
00:02:14,068 --> 00:02:16,260
warm, cozy place.

46
00:02:16,502 --> 00:02:18,346
Come in, come in!

47
00:02:19,438 --> 00:02:22,532
Nina and Popcorn sat down by the fire.

48
00:02:22,729 --> 00:02:26,943
They were given a fluffy blanket,
a mug of warm milk with honey,

49
00:02:26,993 --> 00:02:28,935
and a sweet little bun.

50
00:02:29,572 --> 00:02:31,806
Meanwhile, the queen was thinking.

51
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:35,184
Hmm... is she really a princess?

52
00:02:35,328 --> 00:02:36,373
I know!

53
00:02:36,423 --> 00:02:38,615
I'll give her a little test.

54
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,793
So the queen tiptoed out to the garden.

55
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:45,402
There, she picked up
something very, very small:

56
00:02:45,452 --> 00:02:47,171
a round green pea...

57
00:02:47,341 --> 00:02:49,810
that glowed just a little bit in the dark.

58
00:02:50,948 --> 00:02:53,821
The queen placed the pea
right on top of the bed.

59
00:02:54,158 --> 00:02:57,058
Then, on top of the
pea, she put a mattress.

60
00:02:57,471 --> 00:02:59,246
And another one.

61
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,215
And another one.

62
00:03:01,596 --> 00:03:05,449
A blue mattress, a pink
mattress, a yellow mattress,

63
00:03:05,499 --> 00:03:07,330
a polka-dot mattress...

64
00:03:07,865 --> 00:03:09,487
Shall we count together?

65
00:03:09,815 --> 00:03:10,849
One...

66
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:12,099
two...

67
00:03:12,154 --> 00:03:13,354
three...

68
00:03:13,468 --> 00:03:14,664
four...

69
00:03:14,714 --> 00:03:15,914
five...

70
00:03:16,182 --> 00:03:18,860
all the way up to ten mattresses!

71
00:03:19,237 --> 00:03:24,456
And on top of the mattresses, she
piled ten fluffy feather quilts.

72
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:29,213
The bed was so tall, so very tall, that
you needed a little ladder to climb

73
00:03:29,263 --> 00:03:30,418
up.

74
00:03:30,468 --> 00:03:32,493
Good night, Nina.

75
00:03:32,574 --> 00:03:34,698
Good night, Popcorn,

76
00:03:34,748 --> 00:03:35,960
said the queen.

77
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:37,493
Sleep tight.

78
00:03:38,587 --> 00:03:43,279
Nina climbed up, up, up the little
ladder and lay down at the very top.

79
00:03:43,661 --> 00:03:48,950
Popcorn fell asleep right away, on
a pillow no bigger than a spoon.

80
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:52,503
But Nina... rolled to one side.

81
00:03:52,973 --> 00:03:55,234
Then she rolled to the other side.

82
00:03:55,641 --> 00:03:57,277
She lay on her back.

83
00:03:57,697 --> 00:03:59,375
She lay on her tummy.

84
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:02,578
Something tiny was poking her back.

85
00:04:02,768 --> 00:04:04,113
Poke, poke.

86
00:04:04,806 --> 00:04:05,923
Nina thought,

87
00:04:05,973 --> 00:04:07,334
Oh dear...

88
00:04:07,783 --> 00:04:09,578
I just can't fall asleep.

89
00:04:09,803 --> 00:04:12,255
But the queen has been so kind to me.

90
00:04:12,453 --> 00:04:13,919
I don't want to be rude.

91
00:04:14,575 --> 00:04:19,850
And so she lay there, quiet as
a mouse, until the sun came up.

92
00:04:20,926 --> 00:04:23,312
At breakfast, the queen asked,

93
00:04:23,815 --> 00:04:25,479
Well, Nina?

94
00:04:25,632 --> 00:04:27,296
Did you sleep well?

95
00:04:27,948 --> 00:04:29,653
Nina thought for a moment.

96
00:04:29,858 --> 00:04:32,619
She didn't want to hurt anyone's feelings.

97
00:04:32,796 --> 00:04:35,557
But she didn't want to tell a fib, either.

98
00:04:35,728 --> 00:04:38,878
So she answered slowly and kindly:

99
00:04:39,518 --> 00:04:44,323
Your Majesty, your bed is the most
beautiful bed I have ever seen,

100
00:04:44,373 --> 00:04:46,391
and I'm very thankful.

101
00:04:46,723 --> 00:04:50,242
But to be honest, there was a tiny
little something underneath me...

102
00:04:50,328 --> 00:04:52,505
and I hardly slept at all.

103
00:04:53,132 --> 00:04:55,615
The queen clapped her hands with joy.

104
00:04:56,012 --> 00:05:01,301
Only a true princess could feel a pea
under ten mattresses and ten quilts!

105
00:05:01,543 --> 00:05:05,554
And only a truly good heart
would tell the truth so gently!

106
00:05:06,243 --> 00:05:07,921
Prince Theo laughed.

107
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:09,184
A pea?

108
00:05:09,234 --> 00:05:11,371
A little pea kept you awake all night?

109
00:05:12,457 --> 00:05:15,885
The queen climbed the little
ladder and fetched the pea.

110
00:05:16,234 --> 00:05:19,300
It glowed even brighter in the sunshine.

111
00:05:19,678 --> 00:05:21,791
This is no ordinary pea,

112
00:05:21,841 --> 00:05:23,041
said the queen.

113
00:05:23,091 --> 00:05:24,838
It's a magic seed.

114
00:05:24,984 --> 00:05:30,176
It only grows when it's planted by
someone who tells the truth with kindness.

115
00:05:30,476 --> 00:05:33,195
Would you like to plant it, Nina?

116
00:05:33,809 --> 00:05:38,093
Nina dug a little hole in the
soil, placed the pea inside,

117
00:05:38,143 --> 00:05:39,931
and covered it up gently.

118
00:05:40,278 --> 00:05:43,483
Popcorn sprinkled a little water on top.

119
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:44,877
Splish.

120
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:49,579
And slowly, slowly, a
tiny sprout peeked out.

121
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:52,034
The sprout grew into a plant.

122
00:05:52,202 --> 00:05:56,310
And the plant filled up with
little flowers that, at night,

123
00:05:56,382 --> 00:05:59,018
glowed like tiny stars.

124
00:06:00,095 --> 00:06:05,601
That night, the queen made Nina a low
little bed, with just one mattress —

125
00:06:05,651 --> 00:06:08,898
soft, snug, and with no pea at all.

126
00:06:09,525 --> 00:06:14,647
Outside the window, the star-flowers
in the garden twinkled slowly:

127
00:06:14,711 --> 00:06:16,397
twinkle... twinkle...

128
00:06:16,447 --> 00:06:17,647
twinkle.

129
00:06:18,082 --> 00:06:23,774
Nina lay down, pulled the blanket up
to her chin, and gave a great big yawn.

130
00:06:24,126 --> 00:06:27,068
Popcorn snuggled up close beside her.

131
00:06:27,659 --> 00:06:28,372
Hoo...

132
00:06:28,422 --> 00:06:30,096
good night, Nina,

133
00:06:30,146 --> 00:06:31,740
whispered Popcorn.

134
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:34,105
Good night, Popcorn,

135
00:06:34,155 --> 00:06:35,722
whispered Nina.

136
00:06:36,345 --> 00:06:40,370
And with the calm, happy heart of
someone who has told the truth,

137
00:06:40,428 --> 00:06:42,865
Princess Nina closed her eyes...

138
00:06:42,915 --> 00:06:47,023
and slept all night long, warm and happy.

139
00:06:47,646 --> 00:06:50,574
Now it's your turn to
close your eyes, too.

140
00:06:50,979 --> 00:06:52,179
Good night.

141
00:06:53,363 --> 00:06:54,563
The End.

142
00:06:56,284 --> 00:06:56,997
Hoo...

143
00:06:57,047 --> 00:06:58,071
Psst!

144
00:06:58,121 --> 00:06:59,693
Are you still awake?

145
00:06:59,847 --> 00:07:01,900
Did you like tonight's story?

146
00:07:02,045 --> 00:07:06,612
Nina showed us that telling the
truth kindly is a beautiful thing.

147
00:07:06,898 --> 00:07:09,850
And a calm heart helps us fall asleep.

148
00:07:10,011 --> 00:07:14,317
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

149
00:07:14,613 --> 00:07:19,511
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

150
00:07:19,561 --> 00:07:21,966
for more stories at bedtime.

151
00:07:22,270 --> 00:07:23,470
Hoo...

